      "statusChangeID": "6074c0e16f56f415717c79a1",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "complete",
      "value": "How many bytes each synced variable type takes: It varies- it's roughly the C# data size of the variable, plus an offset of one to four bytes per variable, plus a one to four byte length if appropriate. We've added a way to see the payload size of each variable in a debug view in order for you to see the actuals for this in-client rather than trying to calculate it ahead of time (it's also subject to change so best to have access to the actual data)\nHow many bytes are possible to sync on a single UdonBehaviour: Roughly 200b on a continuous behaviour, and roughly 49kb for a manual sync'd behaviour. This is subject to change, these numbers have been added to the docs.\nWhat happens if you exceed the limits: If you exceed limits it fails to raise the event and should spew errors in the logs. The UdonBehaviour should still work, the network layer isn't really aware that udon exists. The receiver has no idea that an event failed to raise. This has been added to the docs.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-03-18T00:58:35.353Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/udon-networking#data-and-specs is really sparse. Please document the following:\n- How many bytes each synced variable type takes (including variable-length arrays and strings, UTF8 or ASCII)\n- How many bytes are possible to sync on a single UdonBehavior\n- What happens if you exceed the limits (does the sync never happen until you change the variables to not exceed the limits? Does the whole UdonBehavior stop working? is there an error message in the console for the sender? Is there an error message for the receiver?",
